course: dictionary
lesson: 12119
title: One word, many colors
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word colors has more than one meaning, and its spelling depends on where you live. In American English it is spelled «colors». In the UK, Ireland, Canada, Australia and New Zealand it is spelled «colours». The meaning is the same.
explain: As a noun, colors are the things we see, like red, blue and yellow. «Red, blue and yellow are primary colors.» Here colors means the kinds of colour that paints are mixed from.
explain: A team's colors are the colours of its shirts or flag. «The team wore their colors with pride.» Here colors means the uniform, not paint.
explain: As a verb, colors means fills with colour, or changes how you see something. «Sunset colors the sky orange.» To check, swap in paints: «Sunset paints the sky orange» still makes sense, so colors means fills with colour here.
fact: Colors is the US spelling; the UK and many other countries spell it «colours».
fact: Primary colors are red, blue and yellow, and you can mix other colours from them.
fact: White light splits into the colors of the rainbow: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.
fact: «Show your true colors» means showing what you really think or feel.
fact: As a verb, colors can mean influences: «Her worry colors everything she does.»
exercise: «Red, blue and yellow are primary colors.» In this sentence, what are colors? | Paint brushes for art class | A team's shirts and flags | *Kinds of colour that we see | Lines drawn on a page
exercise: «The team wore their colors with pride.» What does colors mean here? | Paints for the walls | *The uniform: the team's shirts and flag | Pencils for drawing | Lights in the stadium
exercise: «Sunset colors the sky orange.» What does colors mean in this sentence? | Hides the stars | Counts the clouds | Removes all the light | *Fills with colour
test: Which spelling is used in the UK? | clrs | *colours | colr | color
test: «Her worry colors everything she does.» What does colors mean here? | Washes things away | Paints the room | Covers things in mud | *Influences how she sees things
exam: Ben says colors can be a noun or a verb. Which sentence uses colors as a verb? | *Ella colors the map with a green pencil | Blue is my favourite colour | The team wore their colors | Red is a primary color
